#### LAYER 4: GOLD (Business-Ready / Serving)

**Purpose:** Pre-aggregated, denormalized, optimized for consumption.

| Decision | Choice | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Table type — Aggregations** | Materialized View | Auto-refreshes; optimizer can rewrite queries to use MV |
| **Table type — Denormalized facts** | Managed Table (via MERGE or CTAS) | Full DML support, complex join logic |
| **Format** | Delta | Always |
| **Table location** | Managed | Full UC governance |
| **Clustering** | `CLUSTER BY (date_key, customer_segment)` | Cluster by dashboard filter columns |
| **Expectations** | Business rules | Revenue > 0, dates in valid range, no orphan keys |
| **CDF** | Optional | Enable if downstream systems need incremental feeds |
| **Optimize schedule** | Weekly `OPTIMIZE` | Compact files for fast dashboard queries |

**Gold — Materialized View (auto-refreshing aggregation):**
```sql
-- Gold: Daily revenue summary — auto-refreshes when silver changes
CREATE OR REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW gold.daily_revenue_summary
COMMENT 'Daily revenue by region and segment - refreshes on trigger'
AS SELECT
    o.order_date,
    c.region,
    c.segment,
    COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS order_count,
    COUNT(DISTINCT o.customer_id) AS customer_count,
    SUM(o.amount) AS total_revenue,
    AVG(o.amount) AS avg_order_value
FROM silver.orders_clean o
JOIN silver.customers_current c
    ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id
GROUP BY o.order_date, c.region, c.segment;
```

**Gold — Managed Table (complex denormalized fact):**
```sql
-- Gold: Customer 360 — built via MERGE for incremental updates
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS gold.customer_360 (
    customer_id BIGINT,
    customer_name STRING,
    segment STRING,
    region STRING,
    lifetime_orders INT,
    lifetime_revenue DECIMAL(14,2),
    first_order_date DATE,
    last_order_date DATE,
    avg_order_value DECIMAL(12,2),
    updated_at TIMESTAMP
)
CLUSTER BY (region, segment)
TBLPROPERTIES ('delta.enableDeletionVectors' = 'true');

-- Incremental MERGE from silver CDF
MERGE INTO gold.customer_360 AS target
USING (
    SELECT
        customer_id,
        COUNT(*) AS lifetime_orders,
        SUM(amount) AS lifetime_revenue,
        MIN(order_date) AS first_order_date,
        MAX(order_date) AS last_order_date,
        AVG(amount) AS avg_order_value
    FROM silver.orders_clean
    GROUP BY customer_id
) AS source
    ON target.customer_id = source.customer_id
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET
    target.lifetime_orders = source.lifetime_orders,
    target.lifetime_revenue = source.lifetime_revenue,
    target.last_order_date = source.last_order_date,
    target.avg_order_value = source.avg_order_value,
    target.updated_at = current_timestamp()
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;
```

