### 4. Compute Selection for Each Layer

| Pipeline Stage | Best Compute | Why | Trigger |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Auto Loader ingestion** | Job Cluster (Photon) | Ephemeral, cost-effective, scales with file volume | `trigger(availableNow=True)` for batch-like |
| **SDP Pipeline (bronze → silver → gold)** | SDP-managed cluster | SDP provisions and manages its own cluster | Triggered (batch) or Continuous (streaming) |
| **Batch MERGE (gold layer)** | Job Cluster (Photon) | Heavy write operation, benefits from Photon | Scheduled via Lakeflow Jobs |
| **Dashboard refresh** | Serverless SQL Warehouse | Instant start, auto-scales for concurrent users | On-demand or scheduled |
| **Ad-hoc SQL analytics** | Serverless SQL Warehouse | Sub-second startup, shared across users | On-demand |
| **ML feature engineering** | All-Purpose Cluster (ML Runtime) | Needs Python + ML libraries | Interactive |
| **Streaming (24/7)** | Job Cluster (always-on) | Dedicated, continuous processing | Continuous trigger |

**Cost optimization pattern:**
```
Ingestion + ETL:     Job Cluster (runs 30 min/day)      → Low cost
SDP Pipeline:        SDP cluster (auto-provisioned)     → Medium cost
Dashboard serving:   Serverless SQL WH (auto-stops)     → Pay per query
Development:         Serverless Compute (auto-stops)    → Pay per use
```

