### 5. Storage & File Format Decision

| Decision | Recommendation | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **File format** | Always Delta | ACID, time travel, skipping, Photon-optimized |
| **Managed vs External** | Managed (default) | UC manages lifecycle; DROP = clean delete |
| **When to use External** | Data shared with non-Databricks tools, regulatory retention, multi-cloud | You control the path; DROP leaves data |
| **Source file format for ingestion** | Accept anything → land as Delta | Auto Loader reads JSON/CSV/Parquet/Avro → writes Delta |
| **Target file size** | 64–256 MB (tables < 1 TB), 256 MB–1 GB (tables > 1 TB) | Balanced read parallelism vs file-open overhead |
| **Compression** | Snappy (default for Parquet/Delta) | Best balance of speed vs compression ratio |

**File format conversion principle:**
```
Source: ANY format (CSV, JSON, Parquet, Avro, XML, ORC)
    │
    │  Auto Loader / COPY INTO
    ▼
Bronze: Delta (always)
    │
    │  Streaming / MERGE / MV
    ▼
Silver: Delta (always)
    │
    │  Aggregation / MERGE
    ▼
Gold: Delta (always)

Rule: Convert to Delta at ingestion. Never store intermediate data as CSV/JSON.
```

