### 9. Production Checklist

| # | Check | Layer | Detail |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Auto Loader in file notification mode | Ingestion | Scales to millions of files |
| 2 | `_rescued_data` column on bronze | Bronze | Captures non-conforming records instead of failing |
| 3 | `_ingestion_timestamp` and `_source_file` on bronze | Bronze | Lineage and debugging |
| 4 | Expectations with `ON VIOLATION DROP ROW` on silver | Silver | Bad data filtered, not propagated |
| 5 | CDF enabled on silver | Silver | Gold reads only changes |
| 6 | Liquid Clustering on silver and gold | Silver/Gold | Adaptive, changeable, no small-file problem |
| 7 | Deletion Vectors on all tables | All | Faster MERGE/UPDATE/DELETE |
| 8 | `OPTIMIZE` scheduled weekly on silver, after each load on gold | Silver/Gold | Compact files for query performance |
| 9 | `VACUUM RETAIN 168 HOURS` scheduled weekly | All | Reclaim storage, don't break concurrent readers |
| 10 | `ANALYZE TABLE` after large gold loads | Gold | Accurate stats for join strategy selection |
| 11 | Materialized Views for dashboard aggregations | Gold | Auto-refresh, query rewrite, fast dashboards |
| 12 | Job retries = 2 with exponential backoff | Orchestration | Handle transient failures automatically |
| 13 | Failure notifications (email + webhook) | Orchestration | Alert on-call immediately |
| 14 | Row-level/column-level security on gold | Governance | PII masking, access control |
| 15 | Unity Catalog tags on all tables | Governance | `quality = bronze/silver/gold`, `owner = team` |
| 16 | Serverless SQL Warehouse for dashboards | Consumers | Instant start, auto-scale, Photon |
| 17 | Checkpoints in separate location from data | Streaming | Prevents accidental deletion |
| 18 | Schema evolution mode = `addNewColumns` on Auto Loader | Ingestion | Handles source schema changes gracefully |
| 19 | Circuit breaker: row count validation between layers | All | Prevents bad data propagation |
| 20 | Delta Sharing for cross-team/external access | Governance | Share without copying data |
